From a0954b1507a0f45f979eed5d350b111dffd76636 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:39:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] CR-BODY: six body types (16 live), the slider table, A
 resets a slider, sliders that do nothing are hidden, and the slider test

Body types 10..15 (Athletic, Gangly, Bean, Brick, Willowy, Bobble): portrait_body.c body_mod is now a 16 x 7 byte table
(112 B, was 120 B) with a head size step column; the classic ten keep their rows and a 0 step. One table (CR_SLIDERS)
gives every slider its range, ends and default (the multiplier of CR-SLIDERX can scale it). A on a slider puts it back to
its default (own undo step), the bar shows the distance from the default with a notch. Sliders that change nothing are not
offered: the horn size without horns, the turkey's six face sliders. test_cr_body.c moves every build slider across its
range on every species and body, every step on the bench, with canary bytes; creator_sliders.txt + tools/slider_shots_check.py
are the runner / GBA / PS1 / Dreamcast twin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xd63cvvRYHgPW3b8GJby1n
